ore, the answer **\'1\' is correct**.\n'], 'condensed_response': '**Condensed scene summary (with character tracking)**  \n\n- **Frames\u202f0613‑0619 (Batch\u202f0‑30)** – The camera opens on a bustling trading floor. Brokers in suits crowd around rows of monitors flashing real‑time stock tickers (NYSE, Dow, S&P\u202f500). A close‑up of a rising stock‑chart (frame\u202f0619) reinforces the financial atmosphere.  \n\n- **Frames\u202f0620‑0622 &\u202f0791‑0802** – The setting shifts to a formal interview studio. A middle‑aged man in a dark jacket, identified by the on‑screen graphic as **Fed Chair Jerome\u202fPowell**, speaks at a podium about monetary policy. Adjacent shots show **Treasury Secretary Janet\u202fYellen** (frames\u202f0791‑0794) delivering a similar briefing. Their expressions are serious; the background is a plain, institutional set.  \n\n- **Frames\u202f1433‑1439** – Exterior shots of a neoclassical government building with a flag‑pole (clearly the **Federal Reserve Building**). The camera pans across the façade, establishing the policy‑making context for the interviewees.  \n\n- **Frames\u202f1440‑1443 &\u202f1703‑1713 (Batch\u202f30‑60)** – A second interview segment features **Neel\u202fKashkari**, President of the Minneapolis Fed, addressing reporters inside a conference room. In the foreground, a large screen displays a Bloomberg ticker (DOW, NASDAQ, FTSE) and live market percentages (frames\u202f1708‑1712).  \n\n- **Frames\u202f2930‑2940** – The focus returns to the trading floor, this time emphasizing a wall of monitors that scroll commodity prices (oil, cocoa) and bond yields, underscoring the breadth of the market coverage.  \n\n- **Frames\u202f4235‑4245 (Batch\u202f60‑78)** – A close‑up of a **Bloomberg newsroom** wall shows scrolling indices and a split‑screen with a graphical chart of the “MOY Index.” The camera then cuts to a seated economist **Mohamed\u202fA.\u202fEl‑Erian** (Allianz chief economic advisor) speaking directly to the camera, his office background filled with books and a discreet world‑map.  \n\n- **Frames\u202f5938‑5948** – The final sequence combines additional Bloomberg ticker overlays with El‑Erian’s commentary, reinforcing the documentary’s focus on macro‑economic analysis. No sports or celebratory elements appear throughout; every visual is anchored in finance, policy, or data‑driven discussion.  \n\n**Overall narrative:** The documentary weaves together three visual strands—(1) the kinetic energy of the trading floor, (2) on‑camera interviews with top U.S. economic policymakers (Powell, Yellen, Kashkari), and (3) expert analysis from a leading economist (El‑Erian)—all framed by continuous displays of market data. This tightly‑controlled, institution‑centric sequence confirms the video’s classification as **Economic/Financial** (answer “1”).', 'failed_images': []}
